WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.010
- All right y'all she's a TV legend.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.010
After 11 years hosting The Today Show,

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.391
she's embracing her next chapter in life.

00:00:06.391 --> 00:00:09.010
You can read all about
it in her new book called

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.220
'It's Never Too Late'.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.720
Make the next act of your life,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.020
the best act of your life.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.350
It comes out today,

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.480
you're going to want to get it.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.560
Joining us on Skype,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.673
please welcome Kathie Lee Gifford y'all.

00:00:19.569 --> 00:00:21.819
(cheering)

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.280
Oh my God I love her.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.850
♪ I'll go and get mine ♪

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.810
♪ I'll wear my old lace ♪

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.910
♪ I'll wear my old leather ♪

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.743
- Hi guys.
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:39.743 --> 00:00:44.110
You win for best entrance ever.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.083
That was amazing.

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:47.622
What are you drinking right now?

00:00:47.622 --> 00:00:49.110
Is that yours?

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.420
- That's my wine baby.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.490
- Your wine is good.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.490
You've given me your wine
before it is so good.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.050
So wait, you just moved to Nashville.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.540
So did you do that to write
songs, I know you write a lot?

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.050
- Is the show going on yet?

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.083
- Yes, this is actually the interview.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.210
- Well then let me get comfortable.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.220
Yeah, no, no.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.840
I moved to Nashville because

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.310
I was working here with Brett James

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.570
on the music for this movie that I wrote

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:21.920
called 'Then Came You' with
the amazing Craig Ferguson.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.520
And so Brett and I were
writing all the music together

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.730
for the movie

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.540
and I was here for almost
a year and I just thought

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.610
why am I so fricking
happy all the time here?

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.670
And I realized, it's the culture,

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.880
it's the creative culture

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.340
but it's also the faith culture here.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.270
It's the kindness of people here

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.100
and the joy that they have.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.090
Nobody's talking about the you know,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.860
after you vote then let's
get together and have a drink

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.040
and write a song.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.890
- I know, I love it.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.840
Have you started a new
chapter of your life?

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.320
Dating life like in Nashville?

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.730
Cause that's a different breed of men

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:57.610
than where you were.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.900
- You know well my husband
has been gone now five years.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.520
I know where he is and
I'll see him someday.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.930
But in the meantime,

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.670
you know I didn't date
until like a year ago.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:07.770
It was about four years.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.090
I just didn't want to.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:09.923
- Yeah.

00:02:09.923 --> 00:02:13.164
- And I was so busy with all
my projects and moving here.

00:02:13.164 --> 00:02:16.050
But about a year ago my friends,

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.340
you know it's always your friends that go

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.280
you've got to get out there.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.113
You know I go,

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.283
Why? I've got a full, rich, good life.

00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:27.290
And so they said, well just have some fun.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.700
So I went out with about maybe four guys

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.923
sweet guys.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.010
I mean, great guys,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.680
they just weren't my guy, you know.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.780
It's gotta be the right guy.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.040
I had the right guy for 31 years

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.080
and I'm not going to settle
for less than that next time.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.410
- Don't do it.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.540
I mean, that's amazing too.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.870
I mean amazing for you,

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.240
but not for maybe all the
men that you might date.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.770
So I think there's a high
bar that's already been set

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.440
and I say you keep it there.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.273
- Yeah.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.310
- So Dolly Parton wrote
the forward for your book.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.350
So how long have y'all been friends?

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.510
- I've known Dolly probably
40 years, maybe more.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.360
I first came to Nashville in 1978.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.380
So do the math, which
I'm not very good at.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.163
I was doing a sitcom called,

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:10.983
what is it called?

00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:13.890
Oh, 'Hee Haw Honeys'
based on the Hee Haw Show.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:17.350
And I met her, I met the Gatlins,

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.070
I met Barbara Mandrell,

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.320
I met Kenny Rogers

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.674
so many wonderful country people

00:03:22.674 --> 00:03:24.690
and fell in love with Nashville,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.180
it was a very different city there

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.710
and loved the culture, loved the music,

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.300
I loved the people.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.990
Everybody just shows up and makes music,

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.200
you know that Kelly.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.033
It's what you do.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:35.866
- Yeah. They love it.

00:03:35.866 --> 00:03:39.300
And it's just an everyday thing.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.940
It's like everyday that ends in Y there.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.440
And I think that's what's so creative

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.300
and it's called music city.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.630
Everybody always says just country music.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.463
It's not though.

00:03:45.463 --> 00:03:46.680
There's rock, there's pop.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.530
There's so many different
genres going on there.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.340
So in your book, you talk
about what happened to you

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.173
at the Super Bowl.

00:03:53.173 --> 00:03:54.006
Can you tell that story?

00:03:54.006 --> 00:03:54.990
Cause I mean,

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.350
I have had to do that at
the Super Bowl as well,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.150
and it is already nerve wracking.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.020
Can you tell everybody what happened?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.700
- Yeah, I was...what year was it?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.480
It was 1990, I think it was six.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.130
I think it was...no 1995.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.070
Super Bowl 29 and I was asked
to sing the national anthem,

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.710
which is a you know a huge honor.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.720
And yet at the same time it's terrifying.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.660
I mean, that goes worldwide
and you don't even want to,

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.530
Barry Manilow had said to
me right before I did it,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.670
he did it the year before.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:26.560
And Barry's been a great
friend through all these years

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.610
and he said, Kathy,

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.390
no matter what you do, do
not look up at the scoreboard

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.490
and look at how many people
are going to be watching.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.323
Don't do it, don't do it.

00:04:33.323 --> 00:04:36.160
- Oh good lord don't tell her that.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.030
- Now I'll tell you the story.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:38.910
It was, you know

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.280
we have something called
final looks in our business

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.320
which is we're ready to go,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.590
hair and makeup get over there

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.820
do whatever final touches
you're going to do.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.410
Cause we're ready.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:49.570
And

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:54.570
so my hairdresser by
mistake does hairspray on me

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.530
and goes in my right eye,

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.810
boom, right in my right eye.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.280
And I'm going blinded from that.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.940
And then my makeup artist is working on me

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.970
on the other side and she has a

00:05:05.698 --> 00:05:06.531
- A wand.

00:05:06.531 --> 00:05:09.460
- A mascara wand boom,
right into my left eye.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.240
So I'm walking out like,

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.383
they had to leave me.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.513
They don't wait for you at the Superbowl.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.160
They're leading me out

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.030
and I can hear that everybody's screaming.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.480
I can hear all this noise

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.800
and I'm going Oh, Jesus,

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.530
help me Jesus, help me.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.870
I get there

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.440
and then of course the
orchestration starts.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.690
You can hear the orchestra, full orchestra

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.242
and it's time for me to
sing of all the lyrics.

00:05:36.242 --> 00:05:38.350
♪ Oh say can you, ♪

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.183
what...see.

00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:42.675
(laughing)

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.740
- Oh my God that's awesome.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.770
So anyway you sent me some
t-shirts with phrases on them.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.100
Can you tell us about these?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.890
Because this is hilarious.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:54.723
So this one says,

00:05:54.723 --> 00:05:57.537
"I'm sorry you must be
confusing for someone

00:05:57.537 --> 00:05:59.200
"who cares what you think"

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.623
Which I'm totally in to.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.544
- I love that one.

00:06:03.544 --> 00:06:05.594
I want to make tons of those.

00:06:05.594 --> 00:06:08.187
- This is actually my
favorite though okay.

00:06:08.187 --> 00:06:13.087
"Don't confuse my
kindness with stupidity."

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.227
I'm looking at you.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:19.080
- Yeah, because it's
like I choose to be kind,

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.310
but I'm not stupid.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.800
- Yes. Let's say it again.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.127
Don't confuse my kindness with stupidity.

00:06:26.127 --> 00:06:28.294
Exactly. It's a good one.

00:06:28.294 --> 00:06:31.310
Okay. So y'all Kathy Lee's new book,

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.677
'It's Never Too Late' is out right now.

